From f9d58496558ddfbb6fa133047a9abbabd5bc8bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:53:14 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Don't drop a multi-source input while a stop
 aborts it

Now that every input stream remembers an abort, a stop during the probe
of a video with an external audio file can fail that file's demuxer.
CDemuxMultiSource::Open() then erased its input from the list that
CInputStreamMultiSource::Abort() may still be going through on the
closing thread.

Give up instead once the multi-source input has been aborted. Abort()
sets that flag before it aborts any child, so a probe the stop ended
always sees it.

Assisted-by: Claude
(cherry picked from commit c28d53a135f5b19b09659df8747fb8c438455ef4)
(cherry picked from commit cab98915c2e51e4f4f8c0e48e52d5d0ccc391ab5)
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxMultiSource.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxMultiSource.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxMultiSource.cpp
index 2bc4a35..3ededb1 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxMultiSource.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxMultiSource.cpp
@@ -131,6 +131,10 @@ bool CDemuxMultiSource::Open(const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream>& pInput)
     DemuxPtr demuxer = DemuxPtr(CDVDFactoryDemuxer::CreateDemuxer((*iter)));
     if (!demuxer)
     {
+      // a stop fails the probe, and Abort() may be going through this list on another thread
+      if (m_pInput->Aborted())
+        return false;
+
       iter = m_pInput->m_InputStreams.erase(iter);
     }
     else
